{"title":"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At a certain beach if it is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef80c3481c7bf79d09a5fa5cda7c0919e0efd644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^{\\circ} F$\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and sunny, then the beach will be crowded. On June 10 the beach was not crowded. What can be concluded about the weather conditions on June 10?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4bd5e590c99814f38a3ab07b905631bd1e51d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{The temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F and it was not sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"480\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1661a0c43b480e0f2c9b21104dc86047b207e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{The temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F or it was not sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"467\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2db072991cbb235d2a86bb96aef171117414221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{If the temperature was at least } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F, then it was sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/157d9d3f84c0b4c2003f4938ffb877d757cbf293.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{If the temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F, then it was sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"472\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf50be23c6434e6c9afbd2b0b9261725d422147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{If the temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F, then it was not sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"499\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The beach not being crowded only means that it is not both hot and sunny. Equivalently, it is either cool or cloudy, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> is correct.\n</p><p>It could be in fact cool and sunny, which would violate <b>(A)</b> and <b>(E)</b>. It could also be cool and cloudy, which would violate <b>(D)</b>, or hot and cloudy, which would violate <b>(C)</b>.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at each of the answer choices:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4bd5e590c99814f38a3ab07b905631bd1e51d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{The temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F and it was not sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"480\" height=\"17\" /> This doesn't include the fact that it can also be either cooler than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0940f0197a980e995f03f9db69ad4a06c4244341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and sunny or the temperature could be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0940f0197a980e995f03f9db69ad4a06c4244341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and not sunny, for the beach not to be crowded, so this is wrong.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1661a0c43b480e0f2c9b21104dc86047b207e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{The temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F or it was not sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"467\" height=\"17\" /> This is always correct, because for the beach to not be crowded,  at least 1 of the following conditions has to be true: \n1. The temperature is cooler than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0940f0197a980e995f03f9db69ad4a06c4244341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />\n2. It is not sunny.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> has both of these, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2db072991cbb235d2a86bb96aef171117414221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{If the temperature was at least } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F, then it was sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" /> This is obviously wrong, because if it was at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0940f0197a980e995f03f9db69ad4a06c4244341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, then it would \nhave to be cloudy (or anything other than not-sunny), for there to not be a crowd.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/157d9d3f84c0b4c2003f4938ffb877d757cbf293.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{If the temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F, then it was sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"472\" height=\"17\" /> This is wrong, because it forgets the fact that it can also be not-sunny, because the temperature is lower than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0940f0197a980e995f03f9db69ad4a06c4244341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, so no matter whether it is sunny, or not-sunny, there will not be a crowd.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf50be23c6434e6c9afbd2b0b9261725d422147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{If the temperature was cooler than } 80^{\\circ} \\text{F, then it was not sunny.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"499\" height=\"17\" /> \nThe same said for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> goes for this choice too, because this statement forgets the fact that it can also be sunny, as it doesn't matter whether it is sunny or not, mainly because the temperature is not viable for the crowd to be in the beach.\n</p><p>This concludes that the answer is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~spacex_fanboy\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B\">2011 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_